  "final_message": "The kanban app is complete and verified. Summary of everything done:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`)\n- Flask API: bearer-token auth (register/login/me), task CRUD, gapless 1-based positions per column, `status`/`priority` filters, counts, validation errors as `{\"error\",\"errors\"}`, SQLite in `./data/kanban.db` (WAL), serves `frontend/dist` with SPA fallback\n- Fixed a build-breaking pip issue: hash-bearing `requirements.lock` as constraints triggers `--require-hashes` on modern pip, which rejected the plain `requirements.txt` pins \u2014 `requirements.txt` now carries the full hashed closure (same pins), so the Dockerfile's exact install command works on any pip version\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, Tailwind v4 + React 19 + TS strict)\n- Board with three columns, HTML5 drag-and-drop reordering/moving, drop indicators, counts, priority filter\n- Auth dialog (login/register), task dialog (create/edit/delete), delete confirmation, session persistence via localStorage, 401 session-expiry handling\n- `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` both clean\n\n**Verified**\n- 49/49 API contract checks pass (auth, CRUD, moves, reorders, gap closing, error codes)\n- Data persists across server restarts; static serving, SPA fallback, JSON 404s all work\n- Exact Dockerfile steps validated: `npm ci` + `npm run build`, and `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` in a clean venv\n\n**README** now documents run commands (Docker + local) and the full API endpoint table.\n\nScratch artifacts cleaned up. Not committed \u2014 say the word if you'd like a commit. The only untestable piece here is `docker build` itself (no docker daemon in this sandbox), but each layer was verified directly.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
